        ],
        "summary": "config_lock had one failure exit for three different situations: a swallowed PermissionError on mkdir (the Windows delete-pending carve-out) meant a lock that could NEVER be created burned the full 10s deadline and then reported the hard-coded 'holder appears alive (see owner.json)' - a contention story for a permissions failure, with no errno, no path, and no owner ever read (issue #340; the reporter's self-reentrancy hypothesis was disproven by a runtime probe and an AST call-graph sweep). And the review-attempt ledger recorded which BACKEND reviewed but not which MODEL - while the receipt already carries model/effort/spec, and the row is where post-hoc analysis reads; the value cannot be re-derived from config because the fallback ladder and codex resume both move it (issue #338, recording half - the fn-183 provenance family simply never considered it).",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "The machinery knew the fact and dropped it - twice"
      },
