        "summary": "ConfigLockUnavailable (subclass of ConfigLockTimeout - every existing except site keeps working) fails FAST when the lock path is absent and mkdir was denied, naming errno/strerror and the parent path; the pre-loop parent mkdir (previously a raw traceback past every handler) wraps to the same class. Real timeouts compose the message from observations: owner facts (pid/host/age) when owner.json was read; owner-absent plus when-it-reclaims when not; denied-while-exists keeps polling (the Windows pending-delete carve-out, preserved and pinned). FileExistsError resets the last-error tracker, so genuine contention can never reach the permission branch. No lock semantics, constants, or config changed.",
        "taskIds": [
          "fn-193-deterministic-diagnostics-honest-lock.1"
        ],
        "title": "config_lock reports what it observed"
